{
  "behaviorVersion": 1,
  "title": "Codex app-server native protocol lifecycle",
  "description": "Observable app-server methods and payload-discriminated item lifecycles for codex-cli 0.164.0. Repeated item/started and item/completed nodes are distinguished by native item.type, not normalized categories. The history lane is the controller-owned attach the adapter performs (thread/start, empty thread/inject_items, thread/resume) and its history reads; client requests appear there as nodes because Codex's deprecationNotice answers the request shape, not a server-side lifecycle. Node confidence applies to the event plus selector claim, not merely to the shared method name.",
  "source": "Vendor-generated experimental app-server schema plus the hermetic census in packages/surface/vendors/codex/findings.md (C1, C8); the file-change and history-hydration branches are the 0.164.0 census scenarios of the same name.",
